{"assets":["/statement-assets/f5cd632fb9764e6331521aaec4918da1473f9d14c79c76df3d89caae52c51f67.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"435","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Special Graph"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem you will need to deal with an "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" grid graph. The graph's vertices are the nodes of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" grid. The graph's edges are all the sides and diagonals of the grid's unit squares."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The figure below shows a "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 × 5"},{"kind":"text","text":" graph. The black lines are the graph's edges, the colored circles are the graph's vertices. The vertices of the graph are painted on the picture for a reason: the coloring is a correct vertex coloring of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 × 5"},{"kind":"text","text":" graph into four colors. A graph coloring is correct if and only if each vertex is painted and no two vertices connected by an edge are painted the same color."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/f5cd632fb9764e6331521aaec4918da1473f9d14c79c76df3d89caae52c51f67.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given the size of the grid graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the colors of some of its vertices. Find any way how to paint the unpainted vertices of the graph in 4 colors to make the final coloring a correct vertex graph coloring. If there is no such correct vertex coloring, say that the answer doesn't exist."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2 ≤ n, m ≤ 1000)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters — the given graph. Each character is either «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"», «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"», «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"», «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"», «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"». Character «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"» means that the corresponding vertex is unpainted, otherwise the character means the color of the vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Assume that all the available colors are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there is no way to get correct vertex coloring of the graph, print 0 in a single line. Otherwise print the colored "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" graph. Print the graph in the same format as in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If multiple answers exist, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 5\n10101\n00020\n01000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"13131\n42424\n31313\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 2\n00\n00\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12\n34\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 2\n11\n00\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The answer to the first sample is shown on the picture (1 — green color, 2 — blue, 3 — dark blue, 4 — pink)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample there exists 4! answers, each of them is considered correct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample two vertices with equal colors are connected. So the correct vertex coloring couldn't be obtained."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"435E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/435/problem/E"}